 "realtime_factor": 0.016014814821623247,
 "text": "Hi, how are you? Light it first with small lighter aquatab, so it' easy to spot under a flashlight. Or use large pocketknife to scrape right behind the lowest hole and start with small twig. Yes, it's easy to spot and doesn't use up useful tool. If the dampness is only on top, you can start with dry grass. Put the smallest ones right at back, they get used long before the big one. Big enough that it stays ablaze for several minutes. Just tea needs much less fire, started with dry herb and fed it until the water runs down. Always put it out completely and give it water before sleep. Pour water on it or smother it with the wet one and cold water it was just started with.",
